{"spec_element": "invariant",
 "proof_obligation": "bridge",
 "diagnosis": "The loop invariants of rolling_max only state |result| == i and m == result[i-1]. They say nothing about m being the maximum of numbers[0..i], or about each result[j] being the maximum of numbers[0..j+1]. So on loop exit (i == |numbers|) the invariants do not imply the postcondition forall i :: 0 < i < |result| ==> isMax(result[i], numbers[0..i+1]). Fix: strengthen the invariants with isMax(m, numbers[0..i]) and forall j :: 0 <= j < i ==> isMax(result[j], numbers[0..j+1])."}
